===BODY===
          <h2>Coast roads and the A8</h2>
          <p>The A8 runs along the Riviera from Aix-en-Provence past Cannes and Nice to the Italian border, with steep sections, tunnels and heavy summer traffic. Down on the coast, narrow streets, hillside villages and tight underground car parks make recovery tricky. Many breakdowns here involve high-performance and classic cars that owners prefer to have repaired by their own specialist at home.</p>

          <h2>Where we collect from</h2>
          <p>We collect from Nice, Cannes, Antibes, Juan-les-Pins, Saint-Tropez, Menton and Monaco, and from villas, hotels, marinas and underground car parks, as long as a transporter can get access or the car can be brought out.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>High-value or classic car?</strong> Tell us when you ask for a quote. We'll plan suitable loading and transport, so the car is handled with care all the way home.</p>
          </div>

          <h2>How it works</h2>
          <p>Send us the location, the make and model, whether it runs, and the UK delivery address. We quote one fixed price for the whole journey, collect the car and bring it back to the UK. We can also deal with the garage, villa caretaker or hotel directly in French.</p>
===FAQ===
Q: How long does it take to bring a car back from Nice?
A: It's one of the longest journeys in France, around 1,200 km to the Channel. We'll give you an expected collection and delivery time with the quote.
Q: Can you collect from Monaco?
A: Yes. Monaco is right next to Nice. Send us the address and a contact who can hand over the keys.
Q: Can you transport a classic or high-value car?
A: Yes. Tell us about the car when you ask for a quote, so we can plan the right loading and transport.
